@tradition crew-welcome-tea
// DRAFT (not baked). New hand's tea for the crew who arrive on a rotation shuttle: the first Friday after they come
// aboard. Needs (plans/trad-notes-seasons.md, "New hand's tea"): when: rotation friday (the first Friday after a
// rotation day), honorees = that shuttle's arrivals ({names}, {first}), and the words dept-of-honoree and
// bunk-of-honoree, like the birthday's department and bunkmates. Works arrivals get their mug in the Works tea corner
// (and replace that Friday's works-tea); everyone else has a cup in the mess after dinner, an hour before the jam.
k: 484
title: New hand's tea
when: rotation friday
at: 18:40-19:30
min: 20
prio: 2
early: 5
cake: yes
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
hold: 1
who: honoree always, dept-of-honoree 80%, bunk-of-honoree 60%, everyone 10%
anim: drink
from: The Wren

== mail
- {names} came aboard on Sunday's shuttle. New hand's tea tomorrow at {time}, in the mess. Come and say hello.

== ask
- New hand's tea for {first} tonight. Be friendly. You remember your first week.   #warm
- Tea for the new hand after dinner. I'm bringing biscuits.

== here
- Welcome aboard, {first}.   #warm
- You'll know your way round by next week. Promise.

== thanks
- You join the tea for {names}. Somebody asks you how your first week went, and you've got stories now.   #warm

== chatter
- Have you met {first} yet? Came aboard on Sunday.
